# DOC-130: narrowly-scoped line-ending safety for files that get piped
# directly into psql on a Linux server. A prior session found (and fixed) a
# real bug where a Windows checkout/write path silently introduced CRLF into
# an applied migration's stored function body. Forcing LF for these two
# extensions prevents a repeat, without touching line-ending behavior for
# any other file type in this repository.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
